<div class="container">
  <header class="lesson-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Reference</p>
    <h1>Drum <em>Rudiments</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">The motor patterns underneath everything you'll ever play. Every rudiment below is rendered as real notation — press play to hear it, then open the full lesson for the build-up, tips, and graduation criteria.</p>
  </header>

  <article class="lesson-prose">
    <p>Rudiments are to drumming what scales are to piano: small, repeatable sticking patterns that turn into fills, grooves, and solos once they're automatic. Work them in order — singles and doubles first, then the paradiddle family, then flams and drags. A practice pad and a metronome are all you need.</p>

